From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:59:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_sn2400_charger: Read IBUS at 7.8 mA per
 LSB

The driver converts the IBUS ADC channel at 10 mA per LSB. iOS 15.8.8's
AppleSN2400Charger (iPhone 6s Plus kernelcache) converts channel 2 as
value * 78 / 10000 A, channel 0 (VBUS) as 25 mV and channels 6 and 10
(VDD_MAIN) as 2.5 V + 10 mV per LSB, which the driver already uses.

On the iPhone 6s Plus the old scale read 640 mA with the input limit at
500 mA (0x09 = 0x29, which iOS writes for 500 mA), 130 mA at 100 mA and
110 mA at 90 mA: all 64, 13 and 11 LSB, which at 7.8 mA are 499, 101
and 86 mA. The battery's +250 mA at 500 mA in agrees with the lower
value. The input limit was right; only the reading was high.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_sn2400_charger.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_sn2400_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_sn2400_charger.c
index def90d99e..31e57028a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_sn2400_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_sn2400_charger.c
@@ -148,7 +148,8 @@ static int sn2400_read_adc(struct sn2400_charger *charger,
 		*result = value * 25000;
 		break;
 	case SN2400_ADC_CHANNEL_IBUS:
-		*result = value * 10000;
+		/* iOS AppleSN2400Charger: 78/10000 A per LSB */
+		*result = value * 7800;
 		break;
 	case SN2400_ADC_CHANNEL_VDD_MAIN:
 		*result = 2500000 + value * 10000;
